    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (65.30) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.78) emerge as our strongest plays, bolstered significantly by park factors and prime lineup placement. **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a massive 14% park boost in his matchup against Singer, which effectively offsets the minor drag of hitting eighth. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s projected role at the top of the lineup (+8% order bonus) combined with the favorable matchup against McGreevy keeps his efficiency high. While **Masyn Winn** (64.02) also projects well, the \"Lineup Pending\" status necessitates caution; should he fall out of the top six, his outlook would require immediate reassessment. **Lawrence Butler** remains a vital piece of the lineup as well, riding a 13% dynamic platoon edge against Cavalli to a strong 61.64 score, proving that even against a competent arm, the right context makes him an elite start.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was leaving **Luis Arraez** (46.36) on the bench. Despite his high floor and contact-oriented profile, the matchup against Miller\u2019s 2.85 xERA creates too much resistance for a player who lacks the high-upside speed profile we are prioritizing to close the gap in stolen bases. The optimizer favored the higher ceiling of **Gavin Sheets** (59.47) and the tactical advantage of our primary outfielders, as the negative SP skill impact on **Luis Arraez** (-19%) pushed him just below the threshold for a start. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the sub-60 scores of **Cal Raleigh** (52.90) and **JJ Bleday** (52.74). **JJ Bleday** specifically is fighting an ugly 14% platoon penalty that keeps his value muted despite the park advantage, while **Cal Raleigh** will need to overcome a poor park factor to provide meaningful value. We are proceeding with this configuration to maximize efficiency across the board, keeping a close eye on any late-breaking wind or weather developments that could shift the projections for the evening games.",
